&nbsp; As an IAM Software Engineer, you’ll focus on Identity Governance and Administration (IGA) solutions. Your work combines technical analysis, platform configuration, low-code implementation, integration, testing, and troubleshooting, with custom coding where needed. You’ll work closely with engineers, architects, consultants, and customer teams to deliver secure, reliable solutions. &nbsp;
You’ll join an engineering delivery team of around 8–12 people, working across customer assignments in two-week sprints, often with a specific sprint focus. Our ‘you build it, you run it’ approach combines implementation, ongoing improvement, and troubleshooting after delivery, supported by senior engineers in your own and neighbouring teams doing similar work. &nbsp;
What you’ll do as a n IAM Software Engineer &nbsp;
Design and deliver IGA solutions that help customers govern access, using standard platform capabilities, low-code tools, and integration standards, with C#, SQL, and APIs where needed. &nbsp;
Translate customer needs into technical designs and engineering tasks, working with architects, security engineers, and customer stakeholders to meet security, compliance, scalability, and maintainability requirements. &nbsp;
Troubleshoot complex IAM issues, identify root causes, and implement lasting improvements that reduce recurrence and security risk. &nbsp;
Improve automation and delivery practices, using PowerShell and CI/CD where appropriate to make implementation and ongoing changes more reliable. &nbsp;
Share knowledge and support junior engineers through mentoring, design sessions, and reviews of configurations, integrations, and code. &nbsp;
The impact you’ll have &nbsp;
Your engineering work will help leading organizations manage access confidently, protect sensitive data, and comply with evolving regulations. By building reliable IAM solutions and improving delivery practices, you’ll contribute to technical strategy and help the team deliver more effectively—strengthening client security and trust in the digital landscape. &nbsp;
What we can offer you &nbsp;
Autonomy in your work and support for your career development. &nbsp;
Permanent, full-time contract (40 hours per week) &nbsp;
Flexible, hybrid working: typically two days per week on location—one at a client site and one at our Waardenburg office. &nbsp;
Work outside normal hours is rare (currently fewer than five occasions per year) and always discussed in advance. &nbsp;
Typically, 5–15 learning days per year for your development, including certifications and events. Training and associated costs are agreed individually rather than through a fixed training budget. &nbsp;
30 days of annual leave: 25 flexible days and 5 fixed company days. &nbsp;
Variable team bonus and annual profit distribution &nbsp;
Mobility budget or company lease car &nbsp;
Private pension scheme &nbsp;
Home office setup budget and monthly remote work allowance &nbsp;
Regular team and company social events &nbsp;
What you’ll bring to the team &nbsp;
Core experience and skills &nbsp;
3–6 years in software or platform engineering, including at least one year designing and implementing IGA solutions such as Omada Identity or Microsoft Entra ID Governance. &nbsp;
Experience in solution design, configuration, API integration, testing, and deployment, using Git and CI/CD pipelines (e.g., Azure DevOps). &nbsp;
Practical C# and SQL experience to troubleshoot and extend IAM solutions where needed. &nbsp;
Strong analytical, design, and problem-solving skills, with a deep understanding of software security and the ability to turn security and compliance requirements into practical solutions. &nbsp;
A relevant bachelor’s degree (e.g., computer science or information security), or equivalent experience. &nbsp;
How you work &nbsp;
Strong collaboration, stakeholder management, and communication skills, with a structured, proactive approach and the ability to drive work independently. &nbsp;
Practical requirements &nbsp;
English at C1 and Dutch at B2 or higher, written and spoken. &nbsp;
Client-site travel is within the Netherlands, with current major clients in the Randstad. You’re able and willing to travel to those sites and our Waardenburg office; no driver’s license is required. &nbsp;
Currently residing in the Netherlands and eligible to work here. &nbsp;
Nice to have &nbsp;
Azure experience. &nbsp;
AI-assisted tools for analysis, configuration, testing, documentation, or coding. &nbsp;
Relevant certifications, e.g., Microsoft Certified: Identity and Access Administrator Associate, Omada Certified Engineer, or CISSP. &nbsp;
About SITS | Traxion &nbsp;
SITS | Traxion specializes in Identity &amp; Access Management, with 24 years of consulting experience and a team of 120 specialists. We work with organizations across sectors, including Schiphol Group, dsm-firmenich, Gemeente Rotterdam, Belastingdienst, E.ON, and Ayvens. &nbsp;
As part of the European IT security group SITS, we combine international collaboration with a flat organizational structure and a respectful, collaborative culture. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
Ready to make an impact and secure Europe’s digital identities? Apply today!
Interested but have questions before applying? Contact to learn more about the role and whether it matches your experience. &nbsp;
&nbsp;
